1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,600
I'm your China Travel Expert.

2
00:00:01,600 --> 00:00:04,000
A mud wall in the desert once guarded all of China.

3
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:06,400
Follow me west, past Dunhuang, into the Gobi.

4
00:00:06,400 --> 00:00:08,800
This is Yumen Pass — the Jade Gate.

5
00:00:08,800 --> 00:00:11,200
Emperor Wu built it around 121 BC.

6
00:00:11,200 --> 00:00:13,600
Every Silk Road caravan squeezed through here.

7
00:00:13,600 --> 00:00:16,000
It was named for the jade that passed through.

8
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:18,400
Double-tap if you'd walk this old road.

9
00:00:18,400 --> 00:00:20,800
Today only rammed earth and a beacon tower remain.

10
00:00:20,800 --> 00:00:23,200
Two thousand years of wind, still standing.

11
00:00:23,200 --> 00:00:26,200
★ Expert Tip: Pair Yumen with Dunhuang's Mogao caves in one trip.

12
00:00:26,200 --> 00:00:28,800
Next stop: China's rainbow mountains. Follow the route.
